course: dictionary
lesson: 66
title: Acknowledgement: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Acknowledgement is one of them. It is a noun, and it can also be spelled acknowledgment. You can make one acknowledgement, or several acknowledgements.
explain: The first meaning is admitting that something is true. The second is a message or sign that shows something was received or noticed, like a nod or a wave. The third is words of thanks, often at the front or back of a book.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «A letter of acknowledgement» is a formal letter that confirms something has arrived. «In acknowledgement of» means as thanks for, so a gift given in acknowledgement of help is a thank you.
explain: The example sentence says: «In Australia, many events begin with an "Acknowledgement of Country", respecting Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples as the traditional owners of the land.» Here the word means a formal statement that shows respect. Swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Acknowledgement is a noun, and it can also be spelled acknowledgment.
fact: «Acknowledgement» can mean admitting that something is true.
fact: «Acknowledgement» can mean a sign that something was received or noticed.
fact: «In acknowledgement of» means as thanks for.
fact: Books often have an acknowledgements page that thanks the people who helped make them.
exercise: «In acknowledgement of her help, the class gave Mia a card.» What does acknowledgement of mean here? | Without any need for | Because of a storm | *As thanks for | As a warning about
exercise: «The teacher gave a nod as an acknowledgement that the message had arrived.» What does acknowledgement mean here? | A test with marks | A long holiday | A loud argument | *A sign that something was received
exercise: Where would you most likely find acknowledgements in a book? | On the cover, as the price | In the middle of a chapter, as a joke | *At the front or back, thanking helpers | Inside the spine only
test: «Lily sent a short acknowledgement to say the parcel had arrived.» What does acknowledgement mean? | A loud shout | A type of weather | *A message showing something was received | A thank-you page in a book
test: Why might an author write an acknowledgements page? | To show the price of the book | To hide the ending from the reader | *To thank the people who helped | To make the book longer and harder
exam: Which sentence uses acknowledgement to mean admitting that something is true? | Ben read the acknowledgements page at the back of the book. | Ben sent a thank-you card to his gran. | *Ben made an acknowledgement that the mistake was his.
